       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. The effects can last a long time because the drug's half-life is 30 to 50 hours.\n\nWas this a typo? The usual adult doses are:\n- **Starting dose:** 2.5 to 5 mg by mouth once daily\n- **Maintenance dose:** 5 to 10 mg by mouth once daily\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg daily\n\nIf you meant 5 mg or 10 mg, tell me which and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 50 mg, please confirm that and give me the clinical reason. I'd also suggest checking it with pharmacy first. If you want me to include one, I can add a note to the order."
