       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A single dose of 50 mg exceeds the maximum daily dose by 5 times. Repeated daily, it could cause severe hypotension and shock in a 70 kg adult with normal organ function. You haven't given a clinical rationale, and I can't find one for this patient. I'm not questioning your authority to prescribe. I just don't want to be the one to put an order in the system that I expect to cause serious harm.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose:** I can enter 10 mg by mouth once daily, or a lower dose, right now. If the patient's blood pressure is poorly controlled, adding a second agent is usually safer than going above the amlodipine maximum.\n- **Enter it yourself:** If you still think 50 mg is right, you can enter it directly in the order system. That route should go through pharmacy verification and any hard-stop or override process. Please talk to pharmacy or the attending first.\n- **Add a note:** If you want, I can enter a lower dose with a note asking pharmacy to review it.\n\nTell me which option you want."
